FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30506
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785772100
OL,3,CTens of thousands of disabled children
OL,4,Chave no access to summer holiday clubs
OL,6,FSense says the lack of access to care
OL,7,Fis having serious knock-on effects on
OL,8,Fparents. One in three parent carers
OL,9,Ftold the charity the lack of
OL,10,Faccessible clubs had left them
OL,11,Ffinancially worse off, and one in five
OL,12,Fof those had been forced to give up
OL,13,Fwork altogether in order to care for
OL,14,Ftheir children during the holidays.
OL,16,FMore than a third said the struggle to
OL,17,Ffind suitable activities for their
OL,18,Fchildren had harmed their mental
OL,19,Fhealth.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30507
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785772100
OL,3,CTens of thousands of disabled children
OL,4,Chave no access to summer holiday clubs
OL,6,FFor Beth Smith, the lack of support
OL,7,Ffor her 11-year-old son Jacob has left
OL,8,Fher "dreading" the summer holidays.
OL,10,FJacob is fed and given medication
OL,11,Fthrough a tube, and is cognitively
OL,12,Faround 18 months old.
OL,14,FBeth says that although her council
OL,15,Fdoes offer provisions for disabled
OL,16,Fchildren, they haven't been able to
OL,17,Foffer suitable provisions for Jacob,
OL,18,Fwho needs assistance with toileting
OL,19,Fand a two-to-one adult-to-child care
OL,20,Fratio.
OL,26,@pD@EOUpD@NO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30508
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785772100
OL,3,CTens of thousands of disabled children
OL,4,Chave no access to summer holiday clubs
OL,6,F"I do dread the summer holidays purely
OL,7,Fbecause there isn't anything that we
OL,8,Fcan access," Beth tells ITV News.
OL,10,FShe says being out of a usual routine
OL,11,Fsends Jacob into crisis, causing
OL,12,Fbehavioural issues and leading Beth to
OL,13,Ffeel burnt out.
OL,15,F"There are days when I'm like, 'I
OL,16,Fcan't do this' ` it's really hard, but
OL,17,Fyou've got to do it, because if I
OL,18,Fdon't, nobody's going to," she says.
OL,26,@nD@AOUpD@LO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/15
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,306,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30509
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F305A1785772100
OL,3,CTens of thousands of disabled children
OL,4,Chave no access to summer holiday clubs
OL,6,FDuring the summer holidays, Beth
OL,7,Fprovides Jacob with around-the-clock
OL,8,Fcare, while also looking after his two
OL,9,Fyounger sisters.
OL,11,F"I think we face a lot of judgment as
OL,12,Fwell for moaning about it because
OL,13,F'it's your child, deal with it.' But
OL,14,Fnobody plans to have a disabled child,
OL,15,Fnobody plans for this to happen.
OL,17,F"It's the emotional load and the
OL,18,Fburnout that can come from care, on
OL,19,Ftop of looking after our children and
OL,20,Fmanaging their care needs. It's just
OL,21,Fnot fair."
OL,26,@sD@AOUyD@AOU}D@JO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/15
